; testing/ holds byte-for-byte compiler output (golden dumps and the
; programs that produced them — see testing/README.md). examples/ holds a
; program written to be READ alongside its own dump (examples/README.md).
; Data only, both for the same reason: a dump's line numbers and character
; ranges must keep matching its source, so neither the formatter nor the
; compiler may touch either directory.

